text: ['All creatures lose flying and islandwalk.', "An-Havva Constable's toughness is equal to 1 plus the number of green creatures on the battlefield.", "As An-Zerrin Ruins enters the battlefield, choose a creature type.\\nCreatures of the chosen type don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.", "As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a land.\\nSearch your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'At end of combat, put a -0/-2 counter on each creature blocking or blocked by Greater Werewolf.', "At the beginning of each player's upkeep, Primal Order deals damage to that player equal to the number of nonbasic lands they control.", "At the beginning of your upkeep, put a currency counter on Trade Caravan.\\nRemove two currency counters from Trade Caravan: Untap target basic land. Activate only during an opponent's upkeep.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Hungry Mist unless you pay {G}{G}.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Koskun Falls unless you tap an untapped creature you control.\\nCreatures can't attack you unless their controller pays {2} for each creature they control that's attacking you.", "Aysen Crusader's power and toughness are each equal to 2 plus the number of Soldiers and Warriors you control.", "Baki's Curse deals 2 damage to each creature for each Aura attached to that creature.", "Bird creatures get +1/+1.\\n{1}{W}: Target Bird creature gains banding until end of turn. (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding a player controls are blocking or being blocked by a creature, that player divides that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", 'Blocking creatures gain first strike until end of turn.', 'Choose two target creatures an opponent controls. That player chooses and sacrifices one of those creatures. Put a -1/-1 counter on the other.', "Clockwork Steed enters the battlefield with four +1/+0 counters on it.\\nClockwork Steed can't be blocked by artifact creatures.\\nAt end of combat, if Clockwork Steed attacked or blocked this combat, remove a +1/+0 counter from it.\\n{X}, {T}: Put up to X +1/+0 counters on Clockwork Steed. This ability can't cause the total number of +1/+0 counters on Clockwork Steed to be greater than four. Activate only during your upkeep.", "Clockwork Swarm enters the battlefield with four +1/+0 counters on it.\\nClockwork Swarm can't be blocked by Walls.\\nAt end of combat, if Clockwork Swarm attacked or blocked this combat, remove a +1/+0 counter from it.\\n{X}, {T}: Put up to X +1/+0 counters on Clockwork Swarm. This ability can't cause the total number of +1/+0 counters on Clockwork Swarm to be greater than four. Activate only during your upkeep.", 'Coral Reef enters the battlefield with four polyp counters on it.\\nSacrifice an Island: Put two polyp counters on Coral Reef.\\n{U}, Tap an untapped blue creature you control, Remove a polyp counter from Coral Reef: Put a +0/+1 counter on target creature.', "Counter target spell. If that spell is countered this way, put it on top of its owner's library instead of into that player's graveyard.", "Creature spells can't be cast.\\nPay 4 life: Destroy Aether Storm. It can't be regenerated. Any player may activate this ability.", 'Creature spells cost {2} more to cast.', 'Creatures with flying get +1/+1.', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nProtection from black", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{0}: Dark Maze can attack this turn as though it didn't have defender. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{U}{U}, {T}: Create a 0/1 blue Plant Wall creature token with defender named Kelp.", "Destroy target nonartifact attacking creature. It can't be regenerated. Create a black Spirit creature token. Its power is equal to that creature's power and its toughness is equal to that creature's toughness. Sacrifice the token at the beginning of the next end step.", 'Dry Spell deals 1 damage to each creature and each player.', 'Each player may draw up to two cards. For each card less than two a player draws this way, that player gains 2 life.', "Enchant creature without flying\\nWhen Roots enters the battlefield, tap enchanted creature.\\nEnchanted creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.", "Enchant creature\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Serra Bestiary unless you pay {W}{W}.\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block, and its activated abilities with {T} in their costs can't be activated.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +0/+2.\\nSacrifice Carapace: Regenerate enchanted creature.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +4/+0.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -0/-1.\\nEnchanted creature can't block creatures with power equal to or greater than the enchanted creature's toughness.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature loses flying.\\nWhenever enchanted creature blocks or becomes blocked by a creature, the other creature gains first strike until end of turn.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhen enchanted creature leaves the battlefield, its controller sacrifices a creature.', 'Enchant creature\\n{1}{B}: Put a -1/-1 counter on enchanted creature.', "Enchant land\\nOrcish Mine enters the battlefield with three ore counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep or whenever enchanted land becomes tapped, remove an ore counter from Orcish Mine.\\nWhen the last ore counter is removed from Orcish Mine, destroy enchanted land and Orcish Mine deals 2 damage to that land's controller.", 'Evaporate deals 1 damage to each white and/or blue creature.', "Exile target card from a graveyard.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', 'First strike, haste', 'First strike, protection from red', 'First strike\\n{T}: Target Dwarf creature gets +2/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn. When that creature leaves the battlefield this turn, sacrifice Heart Wolf. Activate only during combat.', 'Flip a coin. If you win the flip, Winter Sky deals 1 damage to each creature and each player. If you lose the flip, each player draws a card.', 'Flying', 'Flying, protection from red', 'Flying\\nOther Faerie creatures you control get +0/+1.\\n{T}: Other Faerie creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn.', "Flying\\nWhen Giant Albatross dies, you may pay {1}{U}. If you do, for each creature that dealt damage to Giant Albatross this turn, destroy that creature unless its controller pays 2 life. A creature destroyed this way can't be regenerated.", 'Flying\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Baron Sengir this turn dies, put a +2/+2 counter on Baron Sengir.\\n{T}: Regenerate another target Vampire.', 'Flying\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Sengir Bats this turn dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Sengir Bats.', 'Flying\\n{1}{W}: Mesa Falcon gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{2}: Roterothopter gets +1/+0 until end of turn. Activate no more than twice each turn.', 'Green enchantment spells and white enchantment spells cost {2} more to cast.', 'Haste\\n{R}{R}{R}: Regenerate Eron the Relentless.', "Marjhan doesn't untap during your untap step.\\n{U}{U}, Sacrifice a creature: Untap Marjhan. Activate only during your upkeep.\\nMarjhan can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.\\n{U}{U}: Marjhan gets -1/-0 until end of turn and deals 1 damage to target attacking creature without flying.\\nWhen you control no Islands, sacrifice Marjhan.", 'Minotaur creatures get +1/+0.', 'Protection from black', 'Protection from white', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nWhenever Rashka the Slayer blocks one or more black creatures, Rashka gets +1/+2 until end of turn.', "Remove Timmerian Fiends from your deck before playing if you're not playing for ante.\\n{B}{B}{B}, Sacrifice Timmerian Fiends: The owner of target artifact may ante the top card of their library. If that player doesn't, exchange ownership of that artifact and Timmerian Fiends. Put the artifact card into your graveyard and Timmerian Fiends from anywhere into that player's graveyard. This change in ownership is permanent.", "Reveal the top card of target opponent's library. If it's a land, you gain 1 life. Then that player shuffles.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Search your library for a blue instant card, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Serrated Arrows enters the battlefield with three arrowhead counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if there are no arrowhead counters on Serrated Arrows, sacrifice it.\\n{T}, Remove an arrowhead counter from Serrated Arrows: Put a -1/-1 counter on target creature.', "Shroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\n{G}: Until end of turn, Autumn Willow can be the target of spells and abilities controlled by target player as though it didn't have shroud.", 'Target blocking creature gets +3/+1 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -5/-0 until end of turn.', "Target land becomes the basic land type of your choice until end of turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Target player discards two cards, then draws as many cards as they discarded this way.', 'Target player loses all poison counters. Leeches deals that much damage to that player.', 'Trample', "Trample\\nBlack Carriage doesn't untap during your untap step.\\nSacrifice a creature: Untap Black Carriage. Activate only during your upkeep.", 'Vigilance\\nWhenever Ghost Hounds blocks or becomes blocked by a white creature, Ghost Hounds gains first strike until end of turn.', 'When Sengir Autocrat enters the battlefield, create three 0/1 black Serf creature tokens.\\nWhen Sengir Autocrat leaves the battlefield, exile all Serf tokens.', 'Whenever Folk of An-Havva blocks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', "Whenever Joven's Ferrets attacks, it gets +0/+2 until end of turn.\\nAt end of combat, tap all creatures that blocked Joven's Ferrets this turn. They don't untap during their controller's next untap step.", "Whenever Labyrinth Minotaur blocks a creature, that creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Whenever Reef Pirates deals damage to an opponent, that player mills a card.', 'Whenever Root Spider blocks, it gets +1/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn.', "Whenever Rysorian Badger attacks and isn't blocked, you may exile up to two target creature cards from defending player's graveyard. If you do, you gain 1 life for each card exiled this way and Rysorian Badger assigns no combat damage this turn.", 'Whenever Serra Inquisitors blocks or becomes blocked by one or more black creatures, Serra Inquisitors gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', "Whenever Spectral Bears attacks, if defending player controls no black nontoken permanents, it doesn't untap during your next untap step.", "White creatures have plainswalk. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Plains.)", 'You gain X plus 1 life, where X is the number of green creatures on the battlefield.', "You may choose not to untap Giant Oyster during your untap step.\\n{T}: For as long as Giant Oyster remains tapped, target tapped creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step, and at the beginning of each of your draw steps, put a -1/-1 counter on that creature. When Giant Oyster leaves the battlefield or becomes untapped, remove all -1/-1 counters from the creature.", "You may tap or untap target creature. Then that creature's controller may pay {2}{U}. If the player does, they may copy this spell and may choose a new target for that copy.", '{1}{B}, {T}: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', "{1}{B}{B}: Veldrane of Sengir gets -3/-0 and gains forestwalk until end of turn. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", '{1}{G}: Leaping Lizard gets -0/-1 and gains flying until end of turn.', "{1}{R}, {T}: Target Dwarf creature gains mountainwalk until end of turn. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Apocalypse Chime: Destroy all nontoken permanents with a name originally printed in the Homelands expansion. They can't be regenerated.", '{3}, {T}: Regenerate target artifact creature.', '{3}: You may put a Minotaur permanent card from your hand onto the battlefield.', "{4}, {T}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn except by Walls.", '{B}, Exile two creature cards from your graveyard: Create a 1/1 black Skeleton creature token. It has "{B}: Regenerate this creature."\\nWhen Drudge Spell leaves the battlefield, destroy all Skeleton tokens. They can\'t be regenerated.', "{G}: Beast Walkers gains banding until end of turn. (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", '{R}, {T}: Anaba Shaman deals 1 damage to any target.', '{R}{R}{R}, {T}: Destroy target artifact creature.', '{R}{R}{R}, {T}: Destroy target noncreature artifact.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add {B}.\\n{2}, {T}: Add {U} or {R}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add {G}.\\n{2}, {T}: Add {R} or {W}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add {R}.\\n{2}, {T}: Add {B} or {G}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add {U}.\\n{2}, {T}: Add {W} or {B}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add {W}.\\n{2}, {T}: Add {G} or {U}.', '{T}: Another target Minotaur creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{T}: Choose target attacking or blocking creature whose controller controls an Island. Dwarven Sea Clan deals 2 damage to that creature at end of combat. Activate only before the end of combat step.', '{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.\\n{1}{W}{W}, {T}: Target creature gains vigilance until end of turn.', "{T}: Reveka, Wizard Savant deals 2 damage to any target and doesn't untap during your next untap step.", '{T}: Tap target creature with power 2 or less.', '{T}: You may put a Faerie permanent card from your hand onto the battlefield.\\n{2}{G}: Target green creature gains protection from black until end of turn.', '{U}: Regenerate Sea Troll. Activate only if Sea Troll blocked or was blocked by a blue creature this turn.', '{W}, {T}: Abbey Matron gets +0/+3 until end of turn.', '{W}: The next 1 damage that would be dealt to target white creature this turn is dealt to Daughter of Autumn instead.', "{W}{W}, {T}: Prevent the next 4 damage that would be dealt this turn to target creature you control. Tap that creature. It doesn't untap during your next untap step.", '{X}, {T}: The next X damage that would be dealt this turn to target white creature you control is dealt to Hazduhr the Abbot instead.']
flavor: ['"A renegade rallying the rabble does not a true Crusader make."\\n—Irini Sengir', '"A thankless job, and a death sentence besides."\\n—Eron the Relentless', '"All the tortures of my vault of horrors pale in comparison to dealing with those petty Bureaucrats."\\n—Baron Sengir', '"All things must eat, after all. Even the air can hunger."\\n—Gemma, Willow Priestess', '"Beast. Defiler. The source of all my pain."\\n—Ihsan\'s Shade', '"Call it a cost of doing business. The best way to protect against thieves is to hire better thieves."\\n—Eron the Relentless', '"Corpses for crew don\'t sit well with me. Zeki and his dead ship had best keep their distance."\\n—Joskun, An-Havva Constable', '"Could there be a fouler act? No doubt the Baron knows of one."\\n—Autumn Willow', '"Curse Reveka, and curse her coddled conjurers. Their sorcerers\' school shall yet be ours."\\n—Irini Sengir', '"Do not fear adversity. Let your courage be your strength."\\n—Onatah, Anaba Shaman', '"Don\'t these goons have anything better to do?"\\n—Joskun, An-Havva Constable', '"Eron would be much less of a hassle if only he were mortal."\\n—Reyhan, Samite Alchemist', '"Faeries talk all in riddles and tricky bits, \'cept the Nobles. Now, *there\'s* some straight talkers."\\n—Joskun, An-Havva Constable', '"Few master the powers of the earth as well as do the Shamans of the Minotaurs."\\n—Baki, Wizard Attendant', '"Here we go again."\\n—Kakra, Sea Troll', '"I do love the rain . . . but this storm feels somehow wrong, Taysir."\\n—Daria', '"I doubt any Labyrinth Minotaurs still live—but then again, we Minotaurs are stubborn beings."\\n—Onatah, Anaba Shaman', '"I hear Halina\'s got a pony that can count to six—and likes to eat meat."\\n—Chandler', '"I hear there are Bears—or spirits—that guard caravans passing through the forest."\\n—Gulsen, Abbey Matron', '"I never question the Autumn Willow about her motives, not even when she turns people into Lizards. It\'s her way."\\n—Devin, Faerie Noble', '"I would say that our Bureaucrats are no better than vipers—but I shouldn\'t insult the vipers."\\n—Murat, Death Speaker', '"I\'ve seen those Trolls devour a drowning sailor faster than his lungs could fill with water."\\n—Zeki, Reef Pirate', '"If that thief Joven ever shows his head around here again, make sure he leaves without it."\\n—Eron the Relentless', '"If the air must feed, let it take the self-righteous."\\n—Murat, Death Speaker', '"Ihsan, the weak. Ihsan, the fallen. Ihsan, the betrayer. He has brought shame to the Serra Paladins where none existed before. May his suffering equal his betrayal."\\n—Baris, Serra Inquisitor', '"In the face of every one I see the Baron."\\n—Daria', '"It helps you pass the time until you die."\\n—Grandmother Sengir', '"It keeps some out, yes. It also keeps others in!"\\n—Grandmother Sengir', '"It\'s nice to see a sister Dwarf in a position of such power, but why\'d it have to be one of those seafaring muleheads?"\\n—Halina, Dwarven Trader', '"It\'s strange, but I can feel it when the land is corrupted. I understand why the Autumn Willow is so protective."\\n—Daria', '"Joskun and the other Constables serve with passion, if not with grace."\\n—Devin, Faerie Noble', '"Joven, you\'re almost as good a thief as I. But Eron hates you even more."\\n—Chandler', '"Just the place for a picnic."\\n—Murat, Death Speaker', '"Legend says they got a treasure cave, but it don\'t say where to find it."\\n—Zeki, Reef Pirate', '"My soul thirsts for Serra\'s salvation, as does my body for life\'s breath."\\n—Ihsan\'s Shade', '"Never brag about the latest wonder you\'ve created, students. Chandler might be listening."\\n—Reveka, Wizard Savant', '"No dwarf alive can best one of my crew dead."\\n—Zeki, Reef Pirate', '"No one can catch what won\'t be caught."\\n—Kakra, Sea Troll', '"Not all Minotaurs are tribal. Some are freelance."\\n—Eron the Relentless', '"Not someone to pick a fight with, unless you\'re fond of pain."\\n—Halina, Dwarven Trader', '"Now, *that\'s* a fashion statement."\\n—Devin, Faerie Noble', '"Oh, I had a conscience once. But alas, I seem to have forgotten where I put it."\\n—Chandler', '"Oh, they scream, right enough, and plead, too—but the Baron keeps no mercy in his vault of horrors."\\n—Zeki, Reef Pirate', '"One day, or another, perhaps I shall ring my pretty chime . . . loudly, so that all may hear."\\n—Grandmother Sengir', '"Play the song of he who delivered us. Play the song of Feroz."\\n—Onatah, Anaba Shaman', '"Poor, foolish Veldrane. He goes wherever the Baron wills him. One day, he\'ll go to die."\\n—Halina, Dwarven Trader', '"Powders and potions are nothing compared to faith."\\n—Baris, Serra Inquisitor', '"Pretty Falcon, friend to Soraya. Will you send her my greetings?"\\n—Gemma, Willow Priestess', '"Rarely be the prey so haughty as to hunt the hunter."\\n—Baron Sengir', '"Rarely have power and madness been so delightfully wed as they have in our dear Grandmother."\\n—Baron Sengir', '"Serra, like Feroz, is long since dead. But remember, Daria: her spirit shall survive so long as the Homelands do."\\n—Taysir', '"Some delicacies are not to be savored, save by the callous."\\n—Baron Sengir', '"Soon, Serra will return and choose the Abbot\'s successor, else we are lost."\\n—Gulsen, Abbey Matron', '"Soraya speaks with the hunters of the air, as do all of her family line."\\n—Autumn Willow', '"Stray not into the path of darkness, or be lost forever."\\n—Baki, Wizard Attendant', '"Such innocent little birds. They sing a sweet song, sitting on their fragile branch."\\n—Grandmother Sengir', '"Swift as the wind and harder to catch—that\'s the Faeries for you."\\n—Daria', '"That Rhino would fetch us a tidy sum, Joven. Perhaps it\'s time to make it ours."\\n—Chandler', '"That cruel being brings shame to all her fellow Dwarves and misery to all the land. She is Sengir\'s daughter in spirit if not in blood."\\n—Reveka, Wizard Savant', '"That which nourishes can also bind."\\n—Gemma, Willow Priestess', '"The An-Zerrins have served me well, ever since I first killed them."\\n—Baron Sengir', '"The Ancestors are the wisdom of the tribe and the soul of the Homelands. I am eternally in their debt."\\n—Taysir', '"The Autumn Willow cannot be everywhere at once—that\'s what her grandchildren are for."\\n—Gulsen, Abbey Matron', '"The Baron\'s drivers are also driven."\\n—Chandler', '"The Beast Walkers do a great service to Aysen. As humans or as beasts, their heart is yet to Serra true."\\n—Baris, Serra Inquisitor', '"The Inn was ever a steady source of good cheer and kindness. Greatly do I miss it, now that I am gone."\\n—Ihsan\'s Shade', '"The Matrons are kindly souls, but don\'t ask one for an ale."\\n—Halina, Dwarven Trader', '"The Matrons still say Serra is coming back. I bet she never even existed."\\n—Murat, Death Speaker', '"The Roterothopter is as insidious as it is ingenious. It is one of the few creations of our school that I take no pride in."\\n—Baki, Wizard Attendant', '"The Shamans? Ha! They are mere craven cows not capable of true magic."\\n—Irini Sengir', '"The Spirit Crafters sing of all our people. They sing of those lost, of those found, and of those who are yet to be."\\n—Onatah, Anaba Shaman', '"The body is a temple with a foundation of sand."\\n—Autumn Willow', '"The faith of Serra is borne on wings of hope."\\n—Gulsen, Abbey Matron', '"The path of faith is fortunately fraught with failure."\\n—Irini Sengir', '"The people of Aysen built their roads with stones from these wonders. Aliban would be pleased with their ingenuity."\\n—Baki, Wizard Attendant', '"The people of Aysen feed us, and we don\'t kill them. That\'s my kind of truce."\\n—Eron the Relentless', '"The roads to Koskun Keep are mostly safe these days. Mostly."\\n—Joskun, An-Havva Constable', '"The smallest beast can yet have the greatest heart."\\n—Gemma, Willow Priestess', '"The tougher to crack, the sweeter the snack."\\n—Kakra, Sea Troll', '"The wisest of Aysen dwell not in the Abbey, but in the laboratory."\\n—Taysir', '"The wolf-things are no mere beasts, but the lieutenants of the Baron."\\n—Taysir', '"Their definition of \'fair profit\' is certainly novel."\\n—Reveka, Wizard Savant', '"There are those who accept being told what to do, what to think, and what to say. Then there are the Folk of An-Havva."\\n—Reyhan, Samite Alchemist', '"There\'s no trade without trust."\\n—Eron, the Relentless', '"They are the eyes of the Baron, and they know your fears."\\n—Ihsan\'s Shade', '"They wouldn\'t sell their own families—at least, not for cheap."\\n—Zeki, Reef Pirate', '"They\'re not half as fierce if they don\'t see you coming."\\n—Devin, Faerie Noble', '"This party is such fun—but it\'s a shame to mourn just one."\\n—Irini Sengir', '"This town\'s only for good folk. The rest can go to the city."\\n—Joskun, An-Havva Constable', '"Those of faith are those of strength."\\n—Autumn Willow', '"Those who fling spells too quickly should have reason to regret it."\\n—Baki, Wizard Attendant', '"Those who hide in hollow towers would do well to remember the rain."\\n—Reyhan, Samite Alchemist', '"Those who say that Serra is dead have never met the Autumn Willow\'s daughters. They are as kind and as generous as Serra would wish us to be."\\n—Gulsen, Abbey Matron', '"Though Serra has not been seen for twenty years, her Gargoyles still watch over our city and punish the guilty."\\n—Gulsen, Abbey Matron', '"Tread the roads of righteousness, Murat, lest you lose your way and be consumed."\\n—Baris, Serra Inquisitor', '"Um . . . oh . . . what was I saying?"\\n—Reveka, Wizard Savant', '"Until I came to the Floating Isle, I never had to oil the servants."\\n—Baki, Wizard Attendant', '"We must shake her limbs and rattle her brains."\\n—Grandmother Sengir', '"What wizards upset, the land soon rights."\\n—Gemma, Willow Priestess', '"Where our potions and powders fail, perhaps nature will succeed."\\n—Reyhan, Samite Alchemist', '"Wherever water is lacking, all things suffer."\\n—Autumn Willow', '"Who needs a spear? Ya break off the horn, and ya stab the fish with it. Easy!"\\n—Kakra, Sea Troll', '"Without the protection of Feroz\'s Ban, I fear the Homelands are lost."\\n—Daria', '"Would that I could be a Paladin again, but the dead hold no place among their ranks."\\n—Ihsan\'s Shade', '"Ya can eat it or ya can weave it, but ya can\'t fight in it."\\n—Zeki, Reef Pirate', '"Your headstone is the last page in the book of your life."\\n—Murat, Death Speaker', '"Zeki sails with a dead crew not out of villainy, but pragmatism."\\n—Baron Sengir', 'Folk of good heart will always find a home.', "Serra's gift to her people: a symbol of faith and hope.", 'The legacy of Feroz lives on.', 'Treachery and anarchy make poor partners.', 'Where hope has no champion, evil rules all.']
artist: ['Alan Rabinowitz', 'Amy Weber', 'Anson Maddocks', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Christopher Rush', 'Dan Frazier', 'Daniel Gelon', 'David A. Cherry', 'Dennis Detwiller', 'Douglas Shuler', 'Heather Hudson', 'Jeff A. Menges', 'Julie Baroh', 'Kaja Foglio', 'Liz Danforth', 'Margaret Organ-Kean', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Tedin', 'Melissa A. Benson', 'Mike Kimble', 'Nicola Leonard', 'NéNé Thomas', 'Pat Lewis', 'Pete Venters', 'Rob Alexander', 'Susan Van Camp', 'Tom Wänerstrand']
